Regarding the Franke database Richard Sucgang writes:

Jakob and I are planning on moving to the new version of Ref-11 (v4)
which is incompatible in file format to the version currently in the
archives.

In retrospect, we are uncertain if the Ref11 format has proven to be
of any use to anyone. Most correspondence and requests for assistance
revolve around the EndNote version, which is unarguably the most
popular of the literature management programs. The BibTeX format is of
use to some people, and _all_ requests for copies on disk have been
for EndNote format, usually for the Macintosh.

If no one is using the Ref11 format, we would like to discontinue
updates for it. If you use the Ref11 files, please let us know as soon
as possible, and which version you use.

By the way, I am trying to use the public domain lharc compression as
the standard way of saving disk space. The *.lzh files can be
compressed and decompressed on four platforms : Unix, Mac, DOS, and
Amiga. Recently, people who have requested for the database on
Macintosh disks I have included the program MacLHA. Please distribute
it around; sending files on compressed format is faster.

